From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:57:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 78/78] i8086: bestrealrec is TDoubleRec on hosts without
 80-bit Extended

compiler/i8086/cpuinfo.pas declares bestrealrec = TExtended80Rec
unconditionally. The system unit only declares TExtended80Rec when
SUPPORT_EXTENDED or FPC_SOFT_FPUX80 is defined (rtl/inc/mathh.inc), so a
compiler built on a host without 80-bit Extended (aarch64, arm, win64,
...) cannot compile the i8086 code generator:

    cpuinfo.pas(33,18) Error: Identifier not found "TExtended80Rec"

On such hosts bestreal (= extended) is Double, and the i386 and x86_64
cpuinfo units already declare bestrealrec = TDoubleRec there. Do the same
for i8086. Where FPC_HAS_TYPE_EXTENDED is defined, the declaration is
unchanged: on x86_64 the resulting ppc8086 is byte-identical to a build of
the original file with the same line layout.
---
 compiler/i8086/cpuinfo.pas | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler/i8086/cpuinfo.pas b/compiler/i8086/cpuinfo.pas
index 4c63472f..0d376cde 100644
--- a/compiler/i8086/cpuinfo.pas
+++ b/compiler/i8086/cpuinfo.pas
@@ -30,7 +30,11 @@ Interface
 
 Type
    bestreal = extended;
+{$ifdef FPC_HAS_TYPE_EXTENDED}
    bestrealrec = TExtended80Rec;
+{$else}
+   bestrealrec = TDoubleRec;
+{$endif}
    ts32real = single;
    ts64real = double;
    ts80real = extended;
